{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BcwvptBiK8JcigSje",
	"notes": "A Sister of Battle of the Adepta Sororitas: an unaugmented but rigorously trained and utterly devout human warrior-nun, wearing power armour but carrying none of the Astartes' gene-seed enhancements. Point math: ST 12 (+20), DX 13 (+60), IQ 11 (+20), HT 12 (+20) = 120, plus Will +1 (+5) = 125; advantages +42; disadvantages -62; skills +95. Total 200 points, the low end of framework.md's \"Elite human (200-350)\" tier. No psychic abilities here: Sororitas Faith is explicitly not psychic power in Black Library fiction and this template does not touch the separate psyker power library. Add Military/Religious Rank levels for a Sister Superior or Canoness built from this base.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tN3QXAxXz9nDVVmmC",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sororitas training is physically demanding, producing soldiers a step above an ordinary Guardsman.\n\nDesign: ST 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tIKHy45AIQ8ekgHQ0",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Extensive combat drill from a young age in the Order's schola.\n\nDesign: DX 13 (+3), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 60,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": 3
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tFE8WchVOWJp37iM3",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sororitas education is thorough but doctrinally narrow compared to, say, an Inquisitorial acolyte's.\n\nDesign: IQ 11 (+1), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "iq",
					"amount": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tzR5oQz_TU8Umi7mm",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Conditioned for endurance in power armour and prolonged campaigns.\n\nDesign: HT 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tC_jMdt3mH3a1DI9w",
			"name": "Will",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Faith translates mechanically into exceptional force of will as much as raw intellect.\n\nDesign: Will 12 (+1 above the IQ-derived default of 11), 5 pts/level (B16).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 5,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "will",
					"amount": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tOCMMXyu67nc7PSvw",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Drilled reactions under fire.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tZDe2M4p7qvWXtHxl",
			"name": "High Pain Threshold",
			"reference": "B59",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sororitas are consistently written as fighting on through wounds that would stop lesser soldiers.\n\nDesign: Basic Set High Pain Threshold (B59), 10 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "t4AK7wVa5flJxO02X",
			"name": "Act of Faith",
			"local_notes": "Suggested use: once per session per level, the player declares an Act of Faith and the GM narrates a small miracle appropriate to the moment (see lore). Not a substitute for a psychic power; do not stack with psyker abilities from the psyker power library.\n\nLore: A Sister of Battle's prayer answered at the worst possible moment for her enemies: wounds that don't drop her, a bolter that never jams when it matters, a miraculous shrug-off of a wound that should have killed her. Black Library (the Sisters of Battle novels, Dan Abnett's and others' Sororitas fiction) treats these as real and faith-triggered, not psychic — the Orders explicitly reject psychic power as unclean.\n\nDesign: Built, not borrowed, per framework.md: based on Serendipity's shape (B83, \"something goes providentially right when you need it\") but priced down and given an activation cost, because the fictional trigger is \"spend Faith in a moment of crisis,\" which is a real restriction a GM can enforce (limited uses per session/scene, GM's call on the specific effect) rather than Serendipity's unlimited, GM-adjudicated free use. 6 points/level (40% of Serendipity's 15) reflects that Restricted Use / limited-frequency limitation; buy multiple levels for a Sister who can call on this more than once a session. Does not touch the psyker power library — Sororitas Faith is explicitly not psychic power in the fiction, and this trait is built independently of it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Imperium",
				"Adepta Sororitas"
			],
			"points_per_level": 6,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "tiYWePMFzAFjosNdA",
			"name": "Religious Rank",
			"reference": "B29",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Sister of Battle holds rank within her Order's hierarchy from the day she takes vows.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Rank (B29), 5/level.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Ecclesiarchy"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "tZHDvLWm6gFQs3hyY",
			"name": "Fanaticism (The God-Emperor)",
			"reference": "B136",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sororitas devotion is, if anything, the most absolute in the Imperium — the Orders are the Ecclesiarchy's own military arm and recruit specifically for unshakeable faith.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fanaticism (B136), flat -15, taken for \"the Emperor/the Imperial Creed\" as the group/ideal. Not leveled in Basic Set.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "t1cwgAhecJygpFMzS",
			"name": "Duty (Ecclesiarchy)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Battle Sister's or priest's obligation to the Ministorum's chain of command — frequent and binding, but less constantly lethal than Guard or Inquisition service on average (a Sororitas' hazard comes from her *mission*, not baseline garrison duty).\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133), one tier below the fully hazardous, always-on entries above.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Ecclesiarchy"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tTldgpB6Kuv7jPV9T",
			"name": "Vow (Chastity and Poverty)",
			"reference": "B160",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Adepta Sororitas Orders are explicitly convents as much as regiments; Sisters take vows on joining, consistently depicted across Black Library's Sisters of Battle fiction.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Vow (B160/B162's table), a moderate lifestyle-restricting vow, -10.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "t9ITUNnKPJLV9Gk02",
			"name": "Intolerance (Xenos)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"The alien is the enemy\" as baseline Imperial doctrine — not personal bigotry but state religion. Universal across Black Library fiction; only a minority of xenos-sympathetic characters (some Rogue Traders, Ordo Xenos radicals) lack it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140). Costed at -10, the \"very broad category\" end of the range the book allows, since \"all non-human sapient species\" is about as broad a target as Intolerance can name.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tbCdYX39UjNyFf5Rs",
			"name": "Intolerance (Mutants)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"The mutant is the enemy\": Imperial law treats unsanctioned mutation as heresy, and ordinary citizens are shown reporting or lynching mutants on sight (Ciaphas Cain, Gaunt's Ghosts, Necromunda material).\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140), broad-category cost as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tuoz8ttn52tfdZ9kq",
			"name": "Intolerance (Heretics and Psykers)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sororitas doctrine is openly hostile to unsanctioned psychic power as well as heresy — the Orders reject psychic gifts as a temptation to corruption, per their consistent portrayal in Black Library fiction.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140), a combined broad category, -10.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tFupYlfOgbfr8Mam4",
			"name": "Marked by the Order's Habit",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Sororitas is recognisable on sight by her Order's habit and iconography, wherever she goes.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "tUHDtZzBOtCD6EoeI",
			"name": "Never Backs Down From a Fight Against the Unclean",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Retreat from daemons, xenos or heretics is not a Sororitas instinct.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		}
	],
